    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0124" n="104" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg104"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795A.5/6–1350: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Korea </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-13T11:00:00-04:00">June 13, 1950—11
                            a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>576. Pls. clarify urdesp. 456, May 4, 1950<anchor n="1" xml:id="d52-f1"/> stating
                    that “South Korean Army is superior today” to North Korean Army and is better
                    equipped. Intelligence available here as well as most recent KMAG semi-annual
                        report<anchor n="2" xml:id="d52-f2"/> indicate that North Korean airpower
                    and heavier artillery make North Korean armed forces superior and capable of
                    successful operations against South.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d52-f1" n="1" xml:id="d52-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f2" n="2" xml:id="d52-f2-content">
                <p>Reference is to the report for the period ending December 31, 1949, which was
                    transmitted to the Department with despatch no. 99, January 26, from Seoul, not
                    printed (795.58/1–2650).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
